1
00:02:15,466 --> 00:02:19,136
Ryo-san got his first meal in three days.

2
00:02:54,071 --> 00:02:55,172
Wait a moment.

3
00:02:55,639 --> 00:02:57,441
W-What?

4
00:02:58,142 --> 00:02:59,776
I knew it!

5
00:03:01,011 --> 00:03:02,779
Hey! What are you doing?

6
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:04,948
Cut it out, you're creeping me out!

7
00:03:06,116 --> 00:03:07,518
It's the doll. The doll!

8
00:03:08,285 --> 00:03:10,220
I want that doll!

9
00:03:10,454 --> 00:03:11,188
The doll?

10
00:03:12,122 --> 00:03:13,157
You mean this one?

11
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:17,294
This is definitely the early type 2 Bardie...

12
00:03:17,628 --> 00:03:20,364
Please give it to me!

13
00:03:20,564 --> 00:03:22,633
You want this beat-up thing?

14
00:03:22,833 --> 00:03:24,301
I'll buy it at any price!

15
00:03:24,501 --> 00:03:26,236
Just say how much you want!

16
00:03:26,803 --> 00:03:28,205
Name my price, huh...

17
00:03:32,176 --> 00:03:35,345
For 500 yen, I could buy a Makunouchi bento.

18
00:03:35,546 --> 00:03:36,880
Then, 5...

19
00:03:37,114 --> 00:03:38,148
50,000 yen?

20
00:03:39,483 --> 00:03:40,884
For 50,000 yen, I'll pay you in cash!

21
00:03:41,518 --> 00:03:43,554
5, 5, 50,000 yen?!

22
00:03:44,321 --> 00:03:46,857
I had no idea that doll was so valuable.

23
00:03:47,424 --> 00:03:51,828
Even as a guy into action figures like G.I. Joe, I had no idea.

24
00:03:52,029 --> 00:03:53,130
Oh, thank goodness!

25
00:03:53,730 --> 00:03:57,901
Now I've completed my set of early type 2 Ponytail Bardies!

26
00:03:58,135 --> 00:03:59,803
Man-chan is so happy!

27
00:04:01,138 --> 00:04:02,839
Creepy guy...

28
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,341
Who are you?

29
00:04:05,275 --> 00:04:06,143
Me?

30
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:08,278
This is who I am.

31
00:04:08,512 --> 00:04:09,846
A doll critic?

32
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:12,349
Is that an actual job?

33
00:04:13,450 --> 00:04:17,521
If you have any valuable dolls, I'll take them anytime, so come visit me.

34
00:04:18,055 --> 00:04:21,592
Now let's go home and get you cleaned up!

35
00:04:22,059 --> 00:04:25,028
I never thought dolls could be worth that much.

36
00:04:27,831 --> 00:04:29,199
First, let's eat!

37
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,603
Ryo-san got 50,000 yen!

38
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:46,850
No matter how hungry you are, how can you eat so much?

39
00:04:47,551 --> 00:04:50,320
Even a gorilla can't eat this much.

40
00:04:50,921 --> 00:04:51,888
Shut up!

41
00:04:52,089 --> 00:04:55,792
You heartless guys who didn't lend me a penny when I was in trouble!

42
00:04:56,326 --> 00:05:00,964
That's because the chief ordered us not to lend you a single penny.

43
00:05:01,198 --> 00:05:04,668
So will you guys do anything the chief orders you to?

44
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:11,108
Come on, Ryo-chan! It's your fault for spending your paycheck right away!

45
00:05:11,308 --> 00:05:13,076
What's going on here?

46
00:05:13,610 --> 00:05:14,311
Oh, Chief...

47
00:05:14,511 --> 00:05:15,679
Good morning, sir.

48
00:05:16,146 --> 00:05:17,080
Good morning.

49
00:05:17,281 --> 00:05:18,682
Good morning, sir.

50
00:05:21,752 --> 00:05:23,086
R-Ryotsu!

51
00:05:23,453 --> 00:05:25,422
How could you...

52
00:05:25,989 --> 00:05:29,826
You were dead broke three days ago. What's with that lavish meal?!

53
00:05:30,227 --> 00:05:31,828
Did you rob somewhere? Mug someone?

54
00:05:32,062 --> 00:05:32,996
I can't breathe!

55
00:05:33,764 --> 00:05:36,500
Chief, it's not like that! Please calm down!

56
00:05:37,334 --> 00:05:39,169
Ryo-chan, have some tea!

57
00:05:41,905 --> 00:05:43,674
I thought I was gonna die!

58
00:05:46,443 --> 00:05:47,911
Oh, sorry about that.

59
00:05:49,012 --> 00:05:51,014
A law-abiding officer like me

60
00:05:51,248 --> 00:05:54,384
would never resort to burglary or mugging!

61
00:05:54,618 --> 00:05:55,619
Seriously!

62
00:05:56,486 --> 00:06:00,924
Still, I can't believe someone would pay 50,000 yen for a beat-up doll.

63
00:06:01,258 --> 00:06:05,162
There are people like that. Total nerds or hardcore collectors.

64
00:06:05,495 --> 00:06:11,168
TV shows like Antique Appraisers and Treasure Hunting are popular now.

65
00:06:12,536 --> 00:06:14,304
I'm totally stuffed.

66
00:06:14,705 --> 00:06:16,840
Nakagawa, Let's go on patrol!

67
00:06:17,207 --> 00:06:19,743
Huh? What's the rush?

68
00:06:19,976 --> 00:06:22,145
Is it bad for a cop to patrol?

69
00:06:22,345 --> 00:06:24,348
No, no, it's not bad, but...

70
00:06:24,815 --> 00:06:27,484
Then stop complaining and get the car ready!

71
00:06:27,684 --> 00:06:28,585
Sure!

72
00:06:29,986 --> 00:06:34,324
Okay, Sergeant Ryotsu is heading out on patrol!

73
00:06:34,658 --> 00:06:35,492
Y-Yeah...

74
00:06:38,729 --> 00:06:43,734
Ryo-chan volunteering for patrol? Is it gonna snow or something?

75
00:06:47,204 --> 00:06:50,340
Patrol is a lie, of course!

76
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:51,408
What?!

77
00:06:51,608 --> 00:06:55,612
I'm gonna meet the president of a specialty doll company in Koiwa.

78
00:06:55,846 --> 00:06:58,749
Is this about making money?

79
00:06:59,249 --> 00:07:02,252
Of course! Dolls make money!

80
00:07:02,452 --> 00:07:03,787
"TATEISHI TOYS CO., LTD."

81
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:05,922
But it's so quiet.

82
00:07:06,156 --> 00:07:10,761
In the old days, you could hear the machines from a kilometer away.

83
00:07:16,366 --> 00:07:18,235
Hey! Wait!

84
00:07:20,437 --> 00:07:22,272
We don't have a penny left!

85
00:07:22,472 --> 00:07:25,275
Even the machines here have all been seized.

86
00:07:25,475 --> 00:07:27,244
Boss, what's going on?!

87
00:07:27,444 --> 00:07:29,212
Huh? Ryo-san...

88
00:07:29,813 --> 00:07:33,617
We staked the company on last year's Christmas season and made the doll,

89
00:07:33,817 --> 00:07:36,052
but it didn't sell at all.

90
00:07:36,453 --> 00:07:40,223
Debts piled up, I couldn't pay salaries, the staff quit...

91
00:07:40,424 --> 00:07:41,892
We're nearly going bust.

92
00:07:42,426 --> 00:07:44,661
Then what about your old stock?

93
00:07:44,895 --> 00:07:47,831
All taken to pay off loans.

94
00:07:48,064 --> 00:07:49,299
You've gotta be kidding!

95
00:07:49,499 --> 00:07:52,836
What was that doll you bet the company on?

96
00:07:53,403 --> 00:07:54,471
This one.

97
00:07:54,671 --> 00:07:56,640
What are these granny dolls?

98
00:07:56,840 --> 00:08:00,677
It's the Babaffy Doll modeled after the popular group Puffy.

99
00:08:02,946 --> 00:08:06,583
The real ones swing their hips from side to side like a jellyfish,

100
00:08:06,783 --> 00:08:09,686
but these ones are old so their hips bend like this.

101
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:12,489
Who would buy such a stupid thing?

102
00:08:13,156 --> 00:08:16,226
No wonder the company's going under making junk like that!

103
00:08:17,694 --> 00:08:20,063
I thought it would sell...

104
00:08:20,664 --> 00:08:26,169
I'll lose the land and the factory, and my family will be out on the street.

105
00:08:27,437 --> 00:08:29,840
Don't cry. I'll do something about it.

106
00:08:30,073 --> 00:08:33,343
Stop trying to comfort me. The debt is 50 million yen.

107
00:08:33,543 --> 00:08:36,680
There's no way you have that much money.

108
00:08:37,013 --> 00:08:39,182
-Who said I'd lend you the money? -Huh?

109
00:08:39,649 --> 00:08:42,252
I'm gonna come up with a doll that will sell!

110
00:08:42,452 --> 00:08:46,356
Even if it's you, you're a total amateur when it comes to dolls.

111
00:08:46,556 --> 00:08:48,792
You shouldn't make promises so easily.

112
00:08:48,992 --> 00:08:50,193
Don't worry!

113
00:08:50,827 --> 00:08:54,798
I may be an amateur at dolls, but I know how to make money!

114
00:08:54,998 --> 00:08:56,633
I-If you say so...

115
00:08:56,833 --> 00:09:01,872
First, we research the current doll market and find out what's hot right now!

116
00:09:02,105 --> 00:09:02,706
Oh!

117
00:09:02,906 --> 00:09:03,673
"YANO DOLL HOUSE"

118
00:09:03,874 --> 00:09:05,575
Hello there!

119
00:09:07,477 --> 00:09:08,712
Oh, welcome.

120
00:09:09,012 --> 00:09:11,448
I've got to talk to you.

121
00:09:12,015 --> 00:09:13,016
Come this way.

122
00:09:27,764 --> 00:09:30,734
-Did you collect all of these? -Of course.

123
00:09:31,668 --> 00:09:34,738
There are so many G.I. Joe and Combat Joe figures!

124
00:09:34,938 --> 00:09:35,939
Wow!

125
00:09:36,606 --> 00:09:43,313
This is the ultra-rare Japanese soldier from the G.I. Joe military series!

126
00:09:43,513 --> 00:09:47,417
G.I. Joe's Japanese soldier was never released in Japan.

127
00:09:47,617 --> 00:09:50,353
Whoa! You even have the G.I. Nurse!

128
00:09:50,554 --> 00:09:53,924
All this stuff would make any collector drool!

129
00:09:54,157 --> 00:09:57,794
Oh, looks like you have pro-level knowledge about G.I. Joe.

130
00:09:58,028 --> 00:09:58,628
Sure!

131
00:09:58,862 --> 00:10:00,931
You've got a ton of the Bardie series too, huh?

132
00:10:01,164 --> 00:10:01,932
Yeah.

133
00:10:02,499 --> 00:10:07,070
Thanks to what I bought from Ryotsu-san last night, I now have the entire series!

134
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:09,172
Which one did you get from me?

135
00:10:09,573 --> 00:10:10,273
This one.

136
00:10:10,507 --> 00:10:13,109
Oh! She looks brand new!

137
00:10:13,577 --> 00:10:15,946
I gave her some proper maintenance.

138
00:10:17,213 --> 00:10:19,783
Aren't these four the same?

139
00:10:20,216 --> 00:10:21,651
Yeah, they look similar.

140
00:10:21,885 --> 00:10:24,754
An amateur wouldn't be able to tell the difference.

141
00:10:32,062 --> 00:10:36,099
No, if you look closely, the expression and finishes are slightly different.

142
00:10:36,299 --> 00:10:38,201
You can tell the difference...

143
00:10:40,604 --> 00:10:43,607
You've got the makings of a Bardie Maniac!

144
00:10:44,641 --> 00:10:47,377
Your personality flips sometimes!

145
00:10:48,745 --> 00:10:50,814
So, what do you want to talk about?

146
00:10:51,014 --> 00:10:51,748
Oh!

147
00:10:51,948 --> 00:10:55,285
This man is the president of Tateishi Toys.

148
00:10:55,485 --> 00:10:59,089
Ah! That's the company that released Babaffy at the end of last year!

149
00:10:59,856 --> 00:11:01,091
Do you know it?

150
00:11:01,291 --> 00:11:03,626
Of course! I bought one myself.

151
00:11:06,596 --> 00:11:11,034
Even though you're a maniac, how could you buy such a crappy doll?

152
00:11:11,267 --> 00:11:14,404
I also collect some oddities.

153
00:11:14,604 --> 00:11:17,941
But that was a total flop even among enthusiasts.

154
00:11:18,141 --> 00:11:18,775
I knew it...

155
00:11:19,409 --> 00:11:23,013
That doll tanked the company, and now it's on the verge of collapse.

156
00:11:23,513 --> 00:11:24,247
So,

157
00:11:24,714 --> 00:11:29,619
I want to get some advice from you and make a doll that will sell.

158
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,855
I understand.

159
00:11:33,023 --> 00:11:34,591
I'd love to help you!

160
00:11:34,791 --> 00:11:36,359
Oh, thank you!

161
00:11:36,693 --> 00:11:39,629
First, let me hear your idea.

162
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:42,666
Speaking of dolls that will sell from now on,

163
00:11:42,866 --> 00:11:45,168
I think it's got to be action figures.

164
00:11:45,602 --> 00:11:47,504
-Huh? -Action figures?

165
00:11:47,704 --> 00:11:48,671
Action!

166
00:11:56,046 --> 00:11:57,047
No!

167
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:59,616
Not figure skating!

168
00:11:59,816 --> 00:12:04,554
Action figures are dolls with movable joints!

169
00:12:05,221 --> 00:12:07,624
Jeez, amateurs...

170
00:12:07,824 --> 00:12:12,896
By the way, I think G.I. Joe had 21 movable parts, right?

171
00:12:13,396 --> 00:12:17,200
With that, they can't sit on their heels or cross-legged like Japanese people.

172
00:12:17,834 --> 00:12:19,069
That's true.

173
00:12:19,302 --> 00:12:21,538
That's what bothers me.

174
00:12:21,738 --> 00:12:22,472
Totally agree!

175
00:12:22,906 --> 00:12:26,509
With more joints, it would be more fun to make more interesting movements

176
00:12:26,710 --> 00:12:27,577
Exactly!

177
00:12:27,777 --> 00:12:29,579
Yeah, so if we start from there...

178
00:12:31,181 --> 00:12:33,083
Ryotsu is late.

179
00:12:33,750 --> 00:12:37,921
Even Ryo-chan can't make a hot-selling doll in one night.

180
00:12:38,555 --> 00:12:39,956
Who says I can't?

181
00:12:40,757 --> 00:12:41,591
R-Ryo-chan!

182
00:12:41,791 --> 00:12:42,559
Ryotsu!

183
00:12:42,759 --> 00:12:44,661
You dare doubt me!

184
00:12:44,861 --> 00:12:46,763
Nothing is impossible for Kankichi Ryotsu!

185
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:48,131
Oh, that's...

186
00:12:48,364 --> 00:12:49,265
Did you make it?

187
00:12:49,499 --> 00:12:51,768
Brace yourselves! Prepare to be amazed!

188
00:12:52,235 --> 00:12:55,972
The ultimate figure I created... is this!

189
00:12:59,242 --> 00:13:00,276
Th-This is...!

190
00:13:01,077 --> 00:13:02,445
A-Amazing!

191
00:13:03,279 --> 00:13:07,784
Ryo-san got his ticket to success...?

192
00:13:19,929 --> 00:13:22,532
D-Did you make a doll of yourself?

193
00:13:22,732 --> 00:13:25,802
I named it "Sgt. Ryo-san"!

194
00:13:26,169 --> 00:13:27,604
But it's so cute!

195
00:13:27,804 --> 00:13:30,473
I really wanted the face to look just like mine,

196
00:13:30,707 --> 00:13:35,411
but to make it a big hit like Tamagotchi, it has to appeal to teenage girls too.

197
00:13:35,612 --> 00:13:36,946
That's absolutely right!

198
00:13:37,147 --> 00:13:41,317
They say celebrities live by their hair, and dolls by their face.

199
00:13:41,551 --> 00:13:43,086
Hold on, there's more!

200
00:13:43,286 --> 00:13:46,556
This doll has other great functions.

201
00:13:46,756 --> 00:13:48,792
C-Can it sit on its heels?!

202
00:13:48,992 --> 00:13:50,560
Not just that!

203
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,395
It can sit cross-legged too...

204
00:13:53,329 --> 00:13:54,297
Just like this!

205
00:13:54,497 --> 00:13:55,565
Wow!

206
00:13:55,832 --> 00:14:00,770
Even G.I. Joe, the king of action figures, can't pull off moves like this!

207
00:14:00,970 --> 00:14:01,938
Of course not!

208
00:14:02,672 --> 00:14:05,141
G.I. Joe only has 21 movable parts,

209
00:14:05,341 --> 00:14:09,179
but this "Sgt. Ryo-san" has 40!

210
00:14:09,412 --> 00:14:10,446
40?!

211
00:14:16,452 --> 00:14:20,890
I added a joint to the knee hinge, so it can bend this much.

212
00:14:21,124 --> 00:14:23,827
Plus, with three more movable parts here,

213
00:14:24,027 --> 00:14:27,463
it can move in every direction, and even sit cross-legged.

214
00:14:27,664 --> 00:14:28,832
Amazing!

215
00:14:29,032 --> 00:14:31,367
And it can do a full 180-degree split too!

216
00:14:32,335 --> 00:14:33,803
This is revolutionary!

217
00:14:34,003 --> 00:14:36,639
B-But this will cost too much...

218
00:14:36,906 --> 00:14:37,907
You idiot!

219
00:14:38,141 --> 00:14:39,475
Even if it costs more,

220
00:14:39,676 --> 00:14:43,913
being the world's first figure with 40 movable parts is a huge selling point!

221
00:14:44,147 --> 00:14:45,215
Exactly!

222
00:14:45,448 --> 00:14:48,084
Maniacs will definitely buy it no matter the price!

223
00:14:48,318 --> 00:14:49,619
I'm not done yet.

224
00:14:49,819 --> 00:14:51,521
I used the same hinge in the hands,

225
00:14:52,455 --> 00:14:55,525
so it can pinch the eye's inner corners, which was impossible before.

226
00:14:56,092 --> 00:15:00,196
The index finger also moves independently, so you can even stick it in the nose.

227
00:15:00,396 --> 00:15:01,097
Whoa!

228
00:15:01,631 --> 00:15:04,901
It can even perfectly recreate this groveling hand-rubbing gesture.

229
00:15:05,468 --> 00:15:08,872
I-Incredible! This is gonna sell for sure!

230
00:15:09,072 --> 00:15:12,642
Let's get the word out to figure maniacs online.

231
00:15:12,842 --> 00:15:13,843
I'll handle it.

232
00:15:14,043 --> 00:15:15,044
Sounds good!

233
00:15:15,245 --> 00:15:17,881
All right, boss! Get this into production!

234
00:15:18,081 --> 00:15:19,282
Hold on, Ryo-san!

235
00:15:19,515 --> 00:15:23,886
I'd love to, but I don't have a penny to fund it.

236
00:15:24,187 --> 00:15:25,188
Don't worry about it!

237
00:15:25,722 --> 00:15:28,691
Don't you care if his whole family ends up on the streets?

238
00:15:28,892 --> 00:15:31,094
Are you heartless?!

239
00:15:31,294 --> 00:15:33,129
A-All right...

240
00:15:33,363 --> 00:15:36,266
I'll have my company talk to the bank.

241
00:15:36,499 --> 00:15:37,934
Boss, we got the money!

242
00:15:38,401 --> 00:15:39,535
Great!

243
00:15:39,736 --> 00:15:40,603
Now then...

244
00:15:40,837 --> 00:15:42,038
Let's talk my cut!

245
00:15:42,238 --> 00:15:43,106
Y-Yeah.

246
00:15:43,306 --> 00:15:45,842
How about this for my share per figure?

247
00:15:46,042 --> 00:15:47,143
What? This much?

248
00:15:47,377 --> 00:15:50,913
If you don't like it, I can pretend this never happened.

249
00:15:51,114 --> 00:15:52,849
N-No way...

250
00:15:53,149 --> 00:15:55,885
Ryotsu gets real serious when money's involved.

251
00:15:56,085 --> 00:15:57,053
Yeah...

252
00:15:57,253 --> 00:15:59,989
"TATEISHI TOYS CO., LTD."

253
00:16:10,967 --> 00:16:14,070
"NEW RELEASE! SGT. RYO-SAN, WORLD FIRST"

254
00:16:14,570 --> 00:16:18,474
Please line up here for "Sgt. Ryo-san"!

255
00:16:18,975 --> 00:16:20,476
-Thanks for waiting! -Here you go!

256
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:22,312
-I'm next! -Yes, here you are!

257
00:16:22,545 --> 00:16:23,880
Yes, thank you very much!

258
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,548
"A SMASH HIT!"

259
00:16:26,149 --> 00:16:28,918
The Ryo-san doll was a huge hit!

260
00:16:29,118 --> 00:16:31,888
Series 2 and 3 flew off the shelves too!

261
00:16:39,562 --> 00:16:43,099
Today's "President's House Visit" comes to you

262
00:16:43,299 --> 00:16:46,102
from President Tateishi's own building at Tateishi Toys,

263
00:16:46,302 --> 00:16:49,572
where the smash-hit "Sgt. Ryo-san" was born.

264
00:16:50,039 --> 00:16:52,141
President, this is an amazing building.

265
00:16:52,608 --> 00:16:55,845
It's all thanks to "Sgt. Ryo-san".

266
00:16:57,947 --> 00:17:02,952
Incredible. He cleared his debts and built his own company building.

267
00:17:03,152 --> 00:17:05,355
I never imagined it'd be such a hit.

268
00:17:05,922 --> 00:17:10,159
Everyone's got a Ryotsu doll now. I can't stand it.

269
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:13,162
I wonder how much Ryo-chan made off this?

270
00:17:13,830 --> 00:17:16,199
He demanded a hefty cut, after all.

271
00:17:16,399 --> 00:17:19,502
A hundred million... no, maybe a billion yen.

272
00:17:19,702 --> 00:17:20,536
Whaaat?!

273
00:17:29,645 --> 00:17:31,314
Oh, you're...

274
00:17:31,981 --> 00:17:34,817
the butler Ryotsu hired when he won the lottery...

275
00:17:35,018 --> 00:17:37,086
I am Sato, the butler.

276
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:40,256
The master has hired me again.

277
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:43,393
M-Master? You mean...

278
00:17:48,498 --> 00:17:52,235
Ryotsu, what's with that ridiculous outfit?

279
00:17:53,636 --> 00:17:56,239
Please don't call me that, Chief.

280
00:17:56,439 --> 00:17:57,173
What?!

281
00:17:57,907 --> 00:18:01,444
I've decided to quit the police today.

282
00:18:01,677 --> 00:18:03,179
And from now on...

283
00:18:03,379 --> 00:18:04,714
Yes, sir.

284
00:18:05,181 --> 00:18:06,349
Here's his business card.

285
00:18:07,583 --> 00:18:08,584
Vice President...

286
00:18:08,818 --> 00:18:09,719
Planning Manager...

287
00:18:09,919 --> 00:18:10,887
Executive?!

288
00:18:11,087 --> 00:18:12,822
That's right.

289
00:18:13,022 --> 00:18:17,927
So you guys should call me Vice President Ryotsu or Ryotsu-sama.

290
00:18:18,261 --> 00:18:19,896
How dare you!

291
00:18:20,563 --> 00:18:21,597
What's with this money?

292
00:18:21,831 --> 00:18:23,566
A token of my appreciation.

293
00:18:25,001 --> 00:18:29,672
I'm also sending Reiko and Nakagawa on an overseas trip.

294
00:18:29,872 --> 00:18:30,773
No thanks!

295
00:18:31,007 --> 00:18:35,878
If you have this much money, pay back your lottery debt first!

296
00:18:36,078 --> 00:18:38,381
Yeah, you've got a billion yen!

297
00:18:41,017 --> 00:18:43,252
Small-minded people are such a hassle.

298
00:18:43,453 --> 00:18:47,924
I'm not the kind of man who settles for a mere billion or two.

299
00:18:48,124 --> 00:18:50,626
I've invested all my profits in my next project

300
00:18:50,860 --> 00:18:55,131
to make ten... no, a hundred times more!

301
00:18:58,434 --> 00:18:59,635
W-What's this?

302
00:18:59,869 --> 00:19:04,340
This is the next new project I've poured all my profits into.

303
00:19:07,276 --> 00:19:10,179
The world's first life-size action figure!

304
00:19:10,913 --> 00:19:13,716
It's amazing, or maybe creepy...

305
00:19:14,450 --> 00:19:16,118
You can change its expression?

306
00:19:16,319 --> 00:19:18,588
It wasn't possible at 1/6 scale,

307
00:19:18,788 --> 00:19:20,923
but at full scale, it is.

308
00:19:21,324 --> 00:19:25,127
But compared to the 1/6 figure, it's kinda too creepy.

309
00:19:25,461 --> 00:19:26,362
No way!

310
00:19:27,063 --> 00:19:30,199
At full scale, it can even wear real clothes.

311
00:19:30,433 --> 00:19:32,168
That's true, but...

312
00:19:32,368 --> 00:19:36,005
Won't you have to sell it for a crazy high price to make a profit?

313
00:19:36,205 --> 00:19:36,939
That's right.

314
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,674
I set the price at 300,000 yen!

315
00:19:39,142 --> 00:19:40,376
300,000 yen?!

316
00:19:40,743 --> 00:19:41,944
That's way too expensive!

317
00:19:42,144 --> 00:19:44,614
No one will buy it at that price!

318
00:19:44,814 --> 00:19:47,316
I'm telling you, don't do that!

319
00:19:47,517 --> 00:19:51,487
I'll do something and get you back to the police.

320
00:19:51,687 --> 00:19:54,157
Stop!

321
00:19:55,191 --> 00:19:56,392
You amateurs...

322
00:19:57,093 --> 00:19:58,861
Figures are forever!

323
00:19:59,328 --> 00:20:03,332
I'm gonna be the Hill Gates of the doll world.

324
00:20:10,706 --> 00:20:13,509
"WORLD FIRST! LIFE-SIZE RYO-SAN"

325
00:20:13,876 --> 00:20:18,014
The world's first full-scale action figure, "Sgt. Ryo-san",

326
00:20:18,481 --> 00:20:21,217
launching worldwide today.

327
00:20:21,417 --> 00:20:24,020
A life-size Ryo-san figure hits the market.

328
00:20:24,220 --> 00:20:24,987
But...

329
00:20:26,589 --> 00:20:28,424
"ORIGINALLY 300,000 YEN, NOW JUST 100,000 YEN!"

330
00:20:28,658 --> 00:20:29,959
"TODAY ONLY! 19,800 YEN!"

331
00:20:30,159 --> 00:20:31,327
"NOW JUST 3,000 YEN!"

332
00:20:36,666 --> 00:20:39,335
The figure didn't sell at all.

333
00:20:39,535 --> 00:20:44,340
"TATEISHI TOYS CO., LTD."

334
00:20:44,874 --> 00:20:48,044
At this rate, we'll go bankrupt with a mountain of unsold stock!

335
00:20:48,511 --> 00:20:50,246
Ryo-san, do something!

336
00:20:52,081 --> 00:20:53,516
Okay, leave it to me!

337
00:20:53,716 --> 00:20:56,752
"A SMASH HIT!"

338
00:20:56,986 --> 00:21:02,525
"BUDDIES' FIGURE SET NOT SOLD SEPARATELY"

339
00:21:02,892 --> 00:21:04,460
What the heck is this?!

340
00:21:04,694 --> 00:21:06,429
This will definitely sell!

341
00:21:06,629 --> 00:21:07,897
Really?

342
00:21:17,907 --> 00:21:20,910
Being bundled with Ryo-chan feels awful!

343
00:21:21,110 --> 00:21:23,446
Business is all about selling!

344
00:21:23,646 --> 00:21:24,847
Oh, what's that?

345
00:21:25,448 --> 00:21:27,750
There's a line at that shoe store too.

346
00:21:27,950 --> 00:21:28,951
Oh, that one?

347
00:21:29,452 --> 00:21:31,654
That's my Shibuya-style version.

348
00:21:31,887 --> 00:21:34,490
S-Shibuya-style version?!

349
00:21:35,024 --> 00:21:38,294
Bundled with a hot pair of premium sneakers...

350
00:21:38,661 --> 00:21:42,865
Like those old hero-themed snacks with toys inside...

351
00:21:44,267 --> 00:21:46,135
After this, we'll have no stock left!

352
00:21:46,335 --> 00:21:48,404
Boss, let's go to Ginza for a party!

353
00:21:48,604 --> 00:21:51,274
Why not head to Akasaka and drink with geisha!

354
00:21:59,115 --> 00:22:01,250
Come on, Reiko-san, Nakagawa-kun.

355
00:22:01,450 --> 00:22:04,420
-Eat and drink! Enjoy! -Is it really okay to celebrate like this?

356
00:22:04,987 --> 00:22:09,258
Ryotsu's plans never end well...

357
00:22:11,594 --> 00:22:13,996
Yes, this is Nakagawa. What?

358
00:22:14,230 --> 00:22:15,097
A dead body!

359
00:22:16,098 --> 00:22:16,966
What?

360
00:22:20,336 --> 00:22:21,704
Chief, where's the body?

361
00:22:21,937 --> 00:22:23,439
Over there, look!

362
00:22:29,645 --> 00:22:31,314
They're my figures!

363
00:22:31,681 --> 00:22:33,182
W-What's going on?!

364
00:22:33,382 --> 00:22:36,319
Chief, I got a statement from a witness.

365
00:22:36,819 --> 00:22:40,289
Customers who bought the bundled sets with dolls or sneakers

366
00:22:40,489 --> 00:22:42,992
took only the female doll or sneakers,

367
00:22:43,192 --> 00:22:45,361
and threw away the male doll.

368
00:22:45,561 --> 00:22:46,529
What!

369
00:22:46,729 --> 00:22:50,866
They only wanted the Reiko doll or the limited sneakers.

370
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,201
Hey, look!

371
00:22:52,468 --> 00:22:54,370
The dolls are floating in one after another!

372
00:23:00,409 --> 00:23:02,712
"DEAD BODY IS COP DOLL!" "BUNDLED SALES UNDER FIRE!"

373
00:23:02,945 --> 00:23:03,979
"BOYCOTT BEGINS!"

374
00:23:06,349 --> 00:23:08,718
The figures have stopped selling.

375
00:23:13,055 --> 00:23:16,859
If only we'd stuck with the 1/6 scale figures...

376
00:23:22,398 --> 00:23:25,668
I-I never thought it'd be this much...!

377
00:23:25,868 --> 00:23:29,505
I'll make you pay for the cost of figure removal.

378
00:23:29,705 --> 00:23:32,575
N-No way! The company went bankrupt,

379
00:23:32,775 --> 00:23:35,845
and I won't get a single penny...

380
00:23:36,045 --> 00:23:37,980
Don't come crying to me.

381
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:41,083
You're not a cop anymore!

382
00:23:41,317 --> 00:23:43,319
Oh, come on, that was just a joke.

383
00:23:43,519 --> 00:23:44,353
Not my problem!

384
00:23:44,887 --> 00:23:48,357
They said they'll charge you if you don't clear all figures out today.

385
00:23:48,557 --> 00:23:51,026
Make sure you dispose of them properly!

386
00:23:51,527 --> 00:23:53,162
That's insane!

387
00:23:54,930 --> 00:23:57,266
I'm being buried by myself!

388
00:23:57,466 --> 00:23:59,368
Chief!

389
00:24:03,005 --> 00:24:08,844
WILDWATER HOUSEBOAT PANIC
